Those players who become bored with NetHack and try SLASH'EM will see
that SLASH'EM is also quite "balanced and polished", and if you say you
don't like "junk" that "doesn't fit in the game", then you could say
that for NetHack as well.

Firearms in SLASH'EM are nice, but only a few classes can use them
skilfully, and even then it's tedious to carry around those bullets or
rockets, because they become too heavy even with a bag of holding.  The
only time I seriously tried to use firearms was with a rogue, but even
then most of the time I used my normal melee weapons.

Playing Doppelgangers is refreshingly different, but I haven't much
experience with them.  Lycanthropes, on the other hand, are quite hard
to play and considered a challenge; I only managed to win one.

Flame and ice mages were a favourite to play for me.  They can be seen
as fighter-mages, and at the beginning of the game they can have a rough
time.  But once you are past the mid-game and have the quest artifacts,
flame and ice mages are fun to play, becoming quite powerful, what with
wielding to good artifacts in addition to casting high level fire and/or
ice spells.

So no, I don't think SLASH'EM is unbalanced at all.  Maybe SLASH was,
but even then, I liked to play it.

